diff --git a/documentation/changelog.rst b/documentation/changelog.rst
index 2a5ac5cdda..c867861835 100644
--- a/documentation/changelog.rst
+++ b/documentation/changelog.rst
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ New features
 
 Infrastructure / Support
 -------------------------
+* Speed up preparing a storage schedule by validating each device's constraints with vectorised comparisons instead of one ``DataFrame.eval`` per check (from ~25 ms to ~3 ms per device); the helpers ``validate_constraint`` and ``sanitize_expression`` in ``flexmeasures.data.models.planning.storage``, which nothing in FlexMeasures called any more, are removed, with ``validate_constraints`` replacing them [see `PR #2641 <https://www.github.com/FlexMeasures/flexmeasures/pull/2641>`_]
 * Triggers for schedules and forecasts are now always counted per organisation, against one budget that all of its users and assets share, so plans no longer choose what triggers are counted against, and the ``FLEXMEASURES_API_RATE_LIMIT_KEY`` setting is deprecated and ignored. Hosts who set it (or a plan's rate-limit key) to ``account+asset`` or ``user`` may want to raise the trigger rate limit of the affected plans, or ``FLEXMEASURES_API_TRIGGER_RATE_LIMIT``, before upgrading [see `PR #2679 <https://www.github.com/FlexMeasures/flexmeasures/pull/2679>`_]
 * Authorization now uses named permissions granted by code-defined user roles and checked against each resource's ACL. New ``account-reader`` and ``account-data-integrator`` roles support scoped access to home-account resources; the ``consultant`` role grants access only through consultancy ACLs on client accounts. Custom roles explicitly named in an ACL retain access to the four preexisting permissions on matching resources. A data migration assigns ``account-member`` to existing users and provisions the narrower roles. To give an existing user reader or data-integrator access, remove their ``account-member`` role after assigning the new role. Account readers cannot initiate password recovery; an account administrator or consultant can initiate a reset for them. The user page shows each role's description in a tooltip [see `PR #2607 <https://www.github.com/FlexMeasures/flexmeasures/pull/2607>`_]
 * A forecast automation's cycle jobs are held to the sensors the automation was checked against, as the jobs of every other kind of data generator are [see `PR #2699 <https://www.github.com/FlexMeasures/flexmeasures/pull/2699>`_]
